␀ù#␀)␀␀␀ "€H␀€␀␀␀␀€␀€␀€␀‚ÿ␀Appendix D␀: ␀PuTTY hacking guide␀␀Ğ␀␀␀ª␀␀␀¬#␀É#␀&␀␀␀ €U␀€␀␀␀˜€€␀␀‚ÿ␀This appendix lists a selection of the design principles applying to the PuTTY source code. If you are planning to send code contributions, you should read this first.␀␀W␀␀␀(␀␀␀ù#␀ #␀/␀␀␀ .€P␀€␀␀␀␀ã‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.1␀: ␀Cross-OS portability␀␀␀d␀␀␀5␀␀␀É#␀„#␀/␀␀␀ .€j␀€␀␀␀␀ã‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.2␀: ␀Multiple backends treated equally␀␀␀r␀␀␀C␀␀␀ #␀ö#␀/␀␀␀ .€†␀€␀␀␀␀ã»‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.3␀: ␀Multiple sessions per process on some platforms␀␀␀M␀␀␀␀␀␀„#␀C#␀/␀␀␀ .€<␀€␀␀␀␀ã²‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.4␀: ␀C, not C++␀␀␀\␀␀␀-␀␀␀ö#␀Ÿ#␀/␀␀␀ .€Z␀€␀␀␀␀ã³‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.5␀: ␀Security-conscious coding␀␀␀d␀␀␀5␀␀␀C#␀	#␀/␀␀␀ .€j␀€␀␀␀␀ã´‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.6␀: ␀Independence of specific compiler␀␀␀R␀␀␀#␀␀␀Ÿ#␀U	#␀/␀␀␀ .€F␀€␀␀␀␀ãµ‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.7␀: ␀Small code size␀␀␀W␀␀␀(␀␀␀	#␀¬	#␀/␀␀␀ .€P␀€␀␀␀␀ã¶‹ùN€␀␀€␀␀€␀␀‰‚ÿ␀␀Section D.8␀: ␀Single-threaded code␀␀␀r␀␀␀C␀␀␀U	#␀
